The form tab still shows the raw answer – it didn’t create a chart because the request didn’t specify a chart.  
To plot the summer comparison you need to ask with a chart spec, e.g.:

```json
{
  "chart": true,
  "spec": {
    "measures": ["per_km"],
    "group_by": ["road_stretch"],
    "filters": {"season": ["Summer"]}
  }
}
```

Then the system will generate a bar chart for “animals killed per km” for each road stretch in Summer.

**AskUserQuestion**

```json
{
  "questions": [
    {
      "header": "File",
      "multiSelect": false,
      "question": "Found Road kill survey - methods.pdf in My Drive / Ecology / Roads. Open it here to take a look?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Yes, open it",
          "description": "Read only, in a tab here"
        },
        {
          "label": "No",
          "description": "Leave it closed"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

I've opened the form for **Volunteer register** in a new tab (see the "Volunteer register" tab). The checks found **17 problems** in 4 kinds (e.g., mobile numbers not 10-digit, invalid emails, future joining dates).

The original file is unchanged. Would you like to **mark the problems in a copy saved in your Drive**? (A copy will have red cells for problem cells and one comment per kind of problem. You can fix it there or ignore it.)

